Check whether your patch fired anywhere. On fremont:

bash
cd ~/work/ascend/AscendNPU-IR
grep -c "memref.alloc.*?x" ~/mr3160_full.log
grep -oE "memref\.alloc\([^)]*\) *(\{[^}]*\})? *: memref<[^>]*\?[^>]*>" ~/mr3160_full.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20

That shows every dynamic alloc that survives, grouped. Look for any with exactly one ?, since those are the ones your patch could act on.

Then do the A-B comparison properly. The stash and pop happened in the same command block, so nothing was rebuilt in between. To actually compare:

bash
git stash
distrobox enter a5-ubuntu
cd ~/work/ascend/AscendNPU-IR
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
ninja -C build-ubuntu bishengir-compile

Then re-dump to a different filename, exit the container, git stash pop, rebuild again, and diff the alloc lines between the two logs. Only that tells you what your 32 lines changed.

Check disk first, you're accumulating 120M logs:

bash
df -h ~
